;;; Syntax probe — unary-and-nary.
;;;
;;; Arity 1 and arity 4, each with and without provenance: a fact of two
;;; arrows and one of five, each drawn as any fact is, an octagon with an
;;; arrow at its relation and one at each argument (Q-M1f.419).
;;; A derived fact's `:using` lists its premises, each a fact:
;;; `:using ((u a))`. A list of names, `:using (x)`, would name no premise,
;;; a name being no fact, and the grammar refuses it at the parse.
;;;
;;;
;;; One of the eighteen node-kind fixtures. As corpus entries they are
;;; rendered under every parse view and every op, and each rendering is
;;; digested by `corpus_shapes.md5`, so a change to how any of these
;;; shapes is drawn moves a digest. They exist because no *puzzle*
;;; contains these shapes.

(relation u T :why "{?3} is u")
(u a)
(u a :source "(1)")
(quad a b c d)
(quad a b c d :rule mk :using ((u a)))
